      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page ([[write-journal]]) describes how the guarded write path journals prior file state for rollback on failure. \n\nSpecifically, it explains that:\n\n- Before the guarded tool executor overwrites any file, it records that file\u0027s prior state \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a record that it did not exist \u2014 into an in-memory write journal.\n- If the agent run fails (due to turn limits, unrecoverable errors, or denied writes), the journal can roll every recorded write back in reverse order: restoring previous content for existing files and deleting newly created files.\n- This mechanism provides all-or-nothing semantics for writes without needing a database transaction \u2014 the journal itself acts as the transaction log, held in process memory for the duration of a single run.\n- The Query agent never uses the rollback path since it has no write tool, though the journal type exists in the shared agent runtime library.",
      "input_tokens": 5157,
